I think a good start would be deciding that the locked doors would 
work like many locked doors in life: they would be freely openable 
from one side but locked from the other. That way you only have to 
ensure that there is a way to find the key on one side of the door, 
not both sides. If the player teleports past a door, it is just like 
getting a free key.

On the other hand, you could surround locked rooms with walls that 
cannot be passed through by any means, including Xorns and teleports, 
and with ceilings that work similarly to prevent trapdoors. That 
would not substantially alter the game any more than the concept of 
locked doors intends to.


